Subject: quartz: fall back to synchronous I/O and legacy file size for VFS hooks
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Modification date: 2026-10-26

Some visual novel engines and translation patches hook Win32 file APIs to stream
media directly out of archives. These legacy hooks often implement GetFileSize
rather than GetFileSizeEx, and expect synchronous ReadFile/SetFilePointer instead
of kernel overlapped I/O.

When GetFileSizeEx fails on a virtual handle, fall back to GetFileSize and mark
the reader as synchronous. Handle reader requests via synchronous seek and read,
ensuring archive-backed media streams play without failing graph construction.

